    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 17th January 2007, the demolition of the existing side covered walkway and rear w.c., and erection of a single storey side extension to the existing house with 2.10m height, 1.15m width, and a depth of 14.00m running parallel to the main house was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls inside the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the proposed extension has a volume of under 70cubic metres.\r\n"
